REPRO (fresh temp board)
  karr create "T1"
  karr delete 1 --yes
  => Cant call method "remove" on an undefined value at Cmd/Delete.pm line 75

ROOT CAUSE
Cmd/Delete.pm:75 calls $task->file_path->remove. Ref-backed tasks (find_task)
never have file_path set — only Task::write/from_file set it. Same family as
task #4 (archive used $task->save). delete currently cannot delete ANY task on
a refs-first board.

FIX DIRECTION
Persist the deletion through the store like everything else:
BoardStore::delete_task($id) already exists (deletes refs/karr/tasks/ID/data)
and is what serialize_from uses. The file_path unlink belongs, if anywhere,
behind a has_file_path guard for materialized views.

Found by karr-test-writer while probing for task #11. Repo VERSION 0.304.
Fixed in 4218164: delete persists via BoardAccess->delete_task (store/ref level) instead of file_path unlink. Pinned in t/44. Suite 42 files / 247 tests PASS. E2E verified: ref removed, neighbors untouched, interactive n-path preserves.
